    "reading": {
        "body": "Developer relations hiring in AI is concentrated in five openings, and the two at Databricks are the same role posted for Seattle and San Francisco.\n\nThe pattern is a small, senior-skewed sample. Databricks titles both roles \"Sr. Developer Advocate.\" SambaNova's is \"Senior Developer Advocate.\" Lambda's is a developer relations role scoped to enterprise AI. Only the Air Force Academy posting is an academic teaching position, and it is the one listing with a published salary range. Four of the five sit in California or Washington, with one remote-eligible.\n\nFor AI specifically, developer relations is the function that converts a model or platform into something builders can actually use. It is downstream of compute in the sense that these companies sell capacity and tooling, but the data here says nothing about how many such roles exist across the industry, only which five were open on these boards on these dates.\n\nWhat this does not cover: no time series, no comparison to prior months, no pay data except the federal range, and no indication of whether five is high or low for this function. The sources listed include aggregators and a posting-share tracker, but none of their aggregate figures appear in this data.",
